**Key design decisions:**

| Concern | How it's handled |
|---|---|
| **Debounce (300 ms)** | `setTimeout` is cleared and re-set on every `change`; only the final timeout fires the Apex call. |
| **Trim & minimum length** | Value is trimmed before the length check. If < 2 chars the timer is already cleared, the request ID is bumped (invalidating any in-flight response), and results/error are reset. |
| **Out-of-order responses** | A monotonically increasing `_requestId` is captured at call time. The `.then` / `.catch` callbacks compare the captured ID against the current `_requestId`; mismatches are silently discarded. |
| **Error display** | The rejected error object is stored on `@track error`; the template renders `<p class="error">{error.body.message}</p>` only when `error` is truthy. |
| **Component disconnected** | `disconnectedCallback` clears the debounce timer so the Apex call is never initiated. Any already-in-flight response is also neutralised by the `_requestId` guard (and the LWC runtime no-ops updates on disconnected components). |

