        String hhRecordTypeId = [
            SELECT Id
            FROM RecordType
            WHERE SObjectType = 'Account'
              AND DeveloperName = 'HH_Account'
            WITH SECURITY_ENFORCED
        ].Id;

        // Create the household account without setting Name –
        // NPSP's Account/Contact triggers will generate the household name automatically
        Account hh = new Account(RecordTypeId = hhRecordTypeId);
        insert hh;

        // Link every member to the new household and persist in one DML statement
        for (Contact c : members) {
            c.AccountId = hh.Id;
        }
        insert members;

        // Designate the first contact as the household's primary contact
        hh.npe01__One2OneContact__c = members[0].Id;
        update hh;

        return hh.Id;
    }
}
```

**How it works:**

| Step | What happens | Why |
|------|-------------|-----|
| 1 | Validate input | Guard clause per spec |
| 2 | SOQL for `RecordType` by `DeveloperName = 'HH_Account'` | Avoids hard-coding a 15/18-char Id that differs per org |
| 3 | `insert hh` with only `RecordTypeId` set (no `Name`) | NPSP's `Account` trigger recognises the HH record type; the `Contact` trigger then fires the household-naming logic when contacts are linked, producing e.g. *"The Smith Household"* and populating greeting fields |
| 4 | Set `AccountId` on all members, single `insert` | One DML call; after insert each `Contact.Id` is populated |
| 5 | Set `npe01__One2OneContact__c` to `members[0].Id`, `update hh` | Satisfies the "first contact is primary" requirement |
| 6 | Return `hh.Id` | The single household account Id |

No extra accounts are created, no name is set manually, and the only DML statements are two inserts and one update—efficient and safe for the typical small family size this method targets.

