```java
public class OPP_MajorGiftFollowUp_TDTM extends npsp.TDTM_Runnable {

    private static final String STAGE_CLOSED_WON = 'Closed Won';
    private static final Decimal MAJOR_GIFT_THRESHOLD = 5000;
    private static final Integer FOLLOW_UP_DAYS = 3;

    public override npsp.TDTM_Runnable.DmlWrapper run(
        List<SObject> newlist,
        List<SObject> oldlist,
        npsp.TDTM_Runnable.Action triggerAction,
        Schema.DescribeSObjectResult objResult
    ) {
        if (newlist == null || newlist.isEmpty()) {
            return null;
        }

        List<Task> tasksToCreate = new List<Task>();

        if (triggerAction == npsp.TDTM_Runnable.Action.AFTER_INSERT) {
            for (SObject so : newlist) {
                Opportunity opp = (Opportunity) so;
                if (isMajorGift(opp)) {
                    tasksToCreate.add(buildTask(opp));
                }
            }
        }
        else if (triggerAction == npsp.TDTM_Runnable.Action.AFTER_UPDATE) {
            if (oldlist == null || oldlist.isEmpty()) {
                return null;
            }
            for (Integer i = 0; i < newlist.size(); i++) {
                Opportunity newOpp = (Opportunity) newlist[i];
                Opportunity oldOpp = (Opportunity) oldlist[i];
                // Create task only when the opportunity transitions into the qualified state
                if (isMajorGift(newOpp) && !isMajorGift(oldOpp)) {
                    tasksToCreate.add(buildTask(newOpp));
                }
            }
        }

        if (!tasksToCreate.isEmpty()) {
            insert tasksToCreate;
        }

        return null;
    }

    private static Boolean isMajorGift(Opportunity opp) {
        return String.equals(opp.StageName, STAGE_CLOSED_WON)
            && opp.Amount != null
            && opp.Amount >= MAJOR_GIFT_THRESHOLD;
    }

    private static Task buildTask(Opportunity opp) {
        Task t = new Task();
        t.Subject  = 'Major gift thank-you call';
        t.Priority = 'High';
        t.Status   = 'Not Started';
        t.WhatId   = opp.Id;
        t.WhoId    = opp.npsp__Primary_Contact__c;
        t.OwnerId  = opp.OwnerId;
        if (opp.CloseDate != null) {
            t.ActivityDate = opp.CloseDate.addDays(FOLLOW_UP_DAYS);
        }
        return t;
    }
}
```

**Design notes:**

| Concern | How it's addressed |
|---|---|
| **TDTM lifecycle** | Extends `npsp.TDTM_Runnable`, overrides `run`. NPSP's dispatcher calls it only while the Trigger Handler record is active; deactivating it stops execution without any code change. |
| **No Apex trigger** | The class is purely a handler; NPSP's single dispatcher trigger (`npsp.TDTM`) invokes it. |
| **AfterInsert logic** | Any new Opportunity that is Closed Won ≥ 5 000 qualifies immediately (it was never "both of those before"). |
| **AfterUpdate logic** | Compares `newlist[i]` with `oldlist[i]`; a task is created **only** when the record transitions *into* the qualified state (was not both Closed Won ≥ 5 000 before). Re-saving an already-qualified gift does **not** create a duplicate. |
| **SOQL budget (≤ 1)** | **Zero** queries. `Trigger.new` / `Trigger.old` (passed by NPSP's dispatcher) already carry every field needed—`StageName`, `Amount`, `CloseDate`, `OwnerId`, `npsp__Primary_Contact__c`. |
| **DML budget (≤ 1)** | All Tasks are collected into a list and inserted in a **single** `insert` statement. |
| **200-opportunity batch** | The loop is O(n) with no per-record queries or DML, so 200 records stay well within governor limits. |
| **Null safety** | `Amount` is null-checked; `CloseDate` is null-checked before `addDays`; `npsp__Primary_Contact__c` is passed through as-is (Task.WhoId is nullable). |
| **Not asynchronous** | The handler performs its DML synchronously in the same transaction and returns `null` (no `DmlWrapper`), matching the "not asynchronous" registration. |

Looking at the two requirements:

1. **Pin the dependency to the promoted build:** The `fsl-dispatch` dependency on `fsl-scheduling` currently uses `2.3.0.LATEST`. While `LATEST` resolves to the latest *released* version, the safest and most explicit approach to guarantee we never accidentally build against a beta is to pin to the specific promoted build: `2.3.0.6`.

